        "original_id": "c6f67dc8-5bec-5940-87dc-cac3c1533c83",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: O'Halloran Hill, Hallett Cove, Adelaide, South Australia\n- Organizations: Cities of Marion, Onkaparinga\n- Topics: suburbs, local government, geography\n\nFacts:\n- O'Halloran Hill is a suburb in southern Adelaide, South Australia, located 18 km from the city centre via Main South Road.\n- O'Halloran Hill is situated on hills south of the O'Halloran Hill Escarpment, which rises from the Adelaide Plains.\n- O'Halloran Hill is split between the Cities of Marion and Onkaparinga.\n- O'Halloran Hill neighbours Happy Valley, Hallett Cove, Trott Park, and Darlington.\n- Hallett Cove is a coastal suburb in southern Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Hallett Cove has a population of more than 12,000 people.",
